<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Inlet and outlet claim</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>A borehole pump fills the school's water tank in \({@a@}\) hours. The kitchen taps, on their own, empty the full tank in \({@b@}\) hours. The tank is empty, and the pump and the taps are turned on together.</p><p>{@nm@} says: <q>The tank fills in \({@b@} - {@a@} = {@cl@}\) hours.</q></p><p>(a) Which statement is right?</p><p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p><p>(b) How long does the tank take to fill? Give your answer exactly or correct to 1 decimal place.</p><p>[[input:ans2]] hours [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>The outlet takes away its fraction each hour. Each hour the pump adds \(\dfrac{1}{ {@a@} }\) of the tank and the taps remove \(\dfrac{1}{ {@b@} }\), so the tank gains</p><p>\[\frac{1}{ {@a@} } - \frac{1}{ {@b@} } = {@fr(net)@}\]</p><p>of its volume each hour. It fills in \(1 \div {@fr(net)@} = {@fr(tt)@}\) hours[[if test="is(integerp(10000*tt) and not integerp(tt))"]], that is \({@dd(tt)@}\) hours[[elif test="is(not integerp(tt))"]], about \({@dd(r1(tt))@}\) hours[[else]][[/if]][[if test="is(hm(tt)#\"\")"]] (that is {@hm(tt)@})[[/if]].</p><p>{@nm@}'s \({@cl@}\) hours is less than the \({@a@}\) hours the pump needs with the taps off, so it cannot be right: opening the taps can only slow the filling down.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
